{
  "id": "PPA-07",
  "title": "Nitrogen & Sulfur Primary Assimilation",
  "subtitle": "Nitrate and sulfate reduction, GS-GOGAT ammonium incorporation, and cysteine/methionine biosynthesis",
  "caption": "Primary inorganic nitrogen and sulfur assimilation in plants. Soil nitrate is reduced to nitrite in the cytosol by Nitrate Reductase (NIA1/2), transported into the chloroplast, and reduced to ammonium by Nitrite Reductase (NIR1). Ammonium is assimilated into glutamate and glutamine via the coupled GS-GOGAT cycle. Concurrently, imported sulfate is activated by ATP Sulfurylase (APS) and reduced by APR and SiR to sulfide, which is condensed with O-acetylserine by OAS-TL to form cysteine.",
  "species_anchor": "arabidopsis_thaliana",
